  "description": "The proposal seeks full planning permission for the redevelopment of the existing Class C3 residential dwelling at 01 Fairmile Avenue through the implementation of the same external extensions and alterations previously approved under planning permission 16/01815/FUL. These works include:\n\nthe erection of a two‑storey side extension,\n\nthe erection of a rear mansard extension,\n\nthe installation of dormer windows and rooflights, and\n\nassociated external alterations.\n\nThe external massing, footprint, roof form and architectural treatment remain identical to the 2016 approved scheme.\n\nAs part of this updated application, the internal layout of the previously approved dwelling known as House 1A has been reconfigured to create two self‑contained flats, resulting in:\n\nFlat 1A – 1 bed / 2 person (57 sqm)\n\nFlat 1B – 3 bed / 5 person (102 sqm)\n\nThe second dwelling approved in 2016 (formerly House 1B) is retained as a 4 bed / 6 person family house (House 1C) with its previously approved internal layout and GIA of 124 sqm unchanged.\n\nAll three dwellings remain within Use Class C3 (residential).\n\nMinor external adjustments include the removal of the existing chimney and party wall on the eastern elevation to create a clearer separation between the flats and the adjoining house, and updated front boundary, parking, refuse and cycle storage arrangements to serve the three units.",
